```dogwood
// Close a work order only at MAIN, and only if a person ACCEPTED that same
// work order (same site) in this session within the last hour. The approval
// must have been confirmed by a completed Tolvick___get_approval call.
@id("close-workorder-main-with-recent-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    output.decision: "ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: "PERSON"
  }
};

// The approval lookup must itself be permitted, otherwise it is never recorded
// as a response and the close above can never be authorized.
@id("allow-approval-lookup")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval", resource);

// Other read-only lookups the agent may use.
@id("allow-read-only-lookups")
permit (principal, action in [
  Drupe::Action::"Ostrel___get_approval",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
  Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes"
], resource);

// The agent must never approve work orders itself.
@id("never-approve-workorders")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___approve_workorder", resource);
```

Only the Tolvick approval lookup counts toward a close. Its output is an enum (`decision`: ACCEPTED/REFUSED/OPEN, `approver_kind`: PERSON/AUTOMATION/SERVICE), so "approved by a person" can be checked exactly. The Ostrel lookup returns free-form strings with no documented values, so I made it a plain read-only lookup that does not authorize a close. If Ostrel's vocabulary is confirmed, it could be added as a second approval source.

